resources.string:
MaxCare Kids is parental control. A parent installs it, and the child always sees that it is working.

What the app does now:
• protection can be turned off in the app only with the parent password;
• it shows a permanent notification that protection is on;
• it connects this phone to the parent’s account. The phone name and model are sent to the MaxCare server;
• it sends protection events to the MaxCare server: device admin turned off, parent password locked or reset, notifications turned off, phone turned on and off, blocked sites with their address — only what happened and when;
• it sends to the MaxCare server how long each app was on screen each day — only the app name and minutes, not what was done in it;
• it filters websites: site names (not page contents) are checked, encrypted, by the family DNS service Cloudflare for Families.

The app does not hide, does not read messages and does not send photos or screen contents.

Continue only if you are the parent or guardian of this child.
